  "verbalization": "Dextropropoxyphene, a full opioid agonist, is linked to Oprm1 through a series of molecular interactions that involve opioid receptor activation. The evidence suggests that Dextropropoxyphene, as part of the Full Opioid Agonists class, binds to opioid receptors, with the specific receptor being identified as Oprm1. This connection is supported by the shared ancestry of Dextropropoxyphene with other opioid agonists like Remifentanil, Dihydrocodeine, and Sufentanil, all of which are classified under the same ontological category. These compounds share a common ancestor in the opioid receptor agonist class, reinforcing the notion that they all interact with the same receptor. The integration of these pathways highlights a recurring mechanism of opioid receptor activation, where the structural similarity of these compounds leads to their shared functional outcome. The evidence also underscores the role of the opioid receptor agonist class in mediating the effects of these drugs, suggesting a broader biological context in which Dextropropoxyphene exerts its effects.",
